    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0139" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/3–1451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Deputy
                        Representative on the North Atlantic Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spofford</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at London</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d55-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-03-21T19:00:00-05:00">March 21, 1951—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Todep 314. We (State and Defense) consider polit “guidance” wld be accepted as
                    “direction” and hence consider them synonymous. We also consider that civilian
                    control of natl policy in peace time is unquestioned. We believe question of
                    guidance versus direction to be essentially one of semantics. You might usefully
                    refer to Para 15 Part one of DC 24/3<anchor n="2" xml:id="d55-f2"/> which states
                    that council Deputies as only higher NATO polit body in continuous session shld
                    be channel through which polit guidance to mil agencies is funnelled, and point
                    out that language used in this doc was approved by both Defense Comite and
                    Council. You cld also refer to Appeal Provisions in Para 16 Part one DC 24/3
                    which clearly indicate that guidance synonymous with direction, at least for
                    purposes this doc, as otherwise there wld be no need for appeal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d55-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d55-f1-content">
                <p> Knight drafted this telegram and cleared it with Colonel Beebe (Defense) and, in
                    substance, with Bonbright.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d55-f2" n="2" xml:id="d55-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 6, <ref target="#pg70">p. 70</ref>.</p>
